good evening ladies and gentlemen it's  my great pleasure to welcome you to the  41st student academy awards the student  academy awards were created in 1972 as  an extension of the Academy's mission to  engage filmmakers at the college level  support emerging voices and celebrate  the excellent work that is being done by  young filmmakers worldwide that mission  is stronger than ever in addition to  these awards the Academy now presents an  extensive year-round program of grants  educational programs media literacy  outreach special screenings and other  programs all in an effort to cultivate  the next generation of filmmakers who  represent the future of our industry and  our Academy every year more than 500  college and university students from  around the world compete for Student  Academy Awards their films are judged in  five categories animation documentary  narrative alternative and foreign we  present up to three awards in each  category gold silver and bronze which  we'll be revealing on stage tonight I'd  like to thank the 76 Academy members who  served as judges we could not keep up  this wonderful Academy tradition without  their long hours of dedication and I  want to express my heartfelt  congratulations to our student winners  you've joined an elite group of  filmmakers whose ranks include as you  saw Robert Zemeckis John Lasseter Pete  dr. Lauren lazin Trey Parker and Spike  Lee along with many other celebrated  filmmakers who have gone on after  winning student academy awards to earn  more than 46 Oscar nominations  and have won or shared aid Oscars I hope  for each of you your student academy  award is the first step in a very long  and successful career I can speak for  all of us at the academy when I say we  can't wait to see what your futures hold  now I would like to introduce our first  presenter to kick off the night with the  documentary category an actor and  documentary filmmaker himself Adrian  Grenier
 

